        <briefdescription>
<para>Given a key that has all index parts (including primary index parts in case of a secondary index), lookup the corresponding tuple in the LSM tree. </para>        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>The tuple is returned in  with its reference counter elevated.</para><para>Note, this function doesn&apos;t track the result in the transaction read set, i.e. it is up to the caller to call vy_tx_track() if necessary. </para>        </detaileddescription>
